{
 "what": "Cameron Freer's published rows for the conditional quartic stack on github.com/elliotglazer/diophantine-z-q (pull request #23, open when decided; twelve tables of #8 to #20), decided by a non-author with code of its own (Node, BigInt and exact rationals; the packet's checker and tools not fetched, read or run): F the files, T each table and its stated counts, R the rows (text and JSON), S that the table is the sum of the squares of the rows.",
 "undecided": "The theorem (Z is Diophantine in Q) is undecided here, and so is the conditional claim of each pull request of the stack (that the rational zero projection of its quartic is Z, given the inherited arithmetic inputs). This decides one finite identity per table: that the published decimal table is, coefficient by coefficient, the sum of the squares of the published balanced integer rows, with the counts the packet states. That the rows are the compiled source system, and every arithmetic argument, are not decided.",
